3a:["$","p",null,{"children":["The 50071 listener loads\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"example-do-not-use-in-prod-rootca.crt"}]," and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"example-do-not-use-in-prod-key.pem"}],"\nfrom the same directory. They are committed to the repository, self-signed,\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"CN=localhost"}],", and ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"expired in October 2024"}],". Every client must pass\n",["$","code",null,{"children":"--insecure"}]," or equivalent, which is what the repository's own TLS integration\ntest does. No certificate-generation script exists anywhere in the tree; you\nsupply real material yourself."]}]
3b:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h3","id":"there-is-no-authentication-on-anything","children":"Nothing is authenticated"}]
3c:["$","p",null,{"children":["Not a Compose limitation: open-source Forge has no inbound\nauthentication on any service, in any deployment. ",["$","code",null,{"children":"docker-compose.yml"}]," does not\npublish the scheduler's port 50061 at all; the worker reaches it over the\nCompose network by service name. That is the only thing standing between an\nattacker on your network and the ability to register as a worker. Keep it\nthat way."]}]
3d:["$","$L1c",null,{"as":"h3","id":"the-build-is-not-fast","children":"The build is not fast"}]
3e:["$","p",null,{"children":["The ",["$","code",null,{"children":"Dockerfile"}]," compiles Forge from the repository root with Bazel, in a\nthree-stage build, and the final image is a fresh Ubuntu with the binary copied\nin and ",["$","code",null,{"children":"curl"}]," installed. The Ubuntu base is digest-pinned and the bazelisk\ndownload is checksum-verified, so the build is reproducible, but it is a full\nfrom-source build every time the layer cache misses. For repeated use, build once and push the image to a\nregistry your hosts can pull from."]}]
